In general the mass, Q of any substance is related to the Volume 
V through the formula:
Q=ρV,   where ρ is the material density
Therefore the mass of pre-fabricated pile is given by:
Q= (24kN/m3) × 0.106m3
Q=254.4 Kg  [assume 1KN =100Kg]
Total embodied energy EE = Q × Iee (Also see computation 
models in Abanda et al. 2012)
EE = 254.4 Kg × (2MJ/Kg)
EE = 508.8 MJ
Total embodied carbon EC = M × ICO2
EC = 254.4 Kg × (0.22KgCO2/Kg)    
EC = 55.97 KgCO2
